# LabVIEW VI Description File for Micromotion Controller
# This file describes the structure and functionality of the LabVIEW module

VI_NAME: "Micromotion_Controller_LabVIEW"
VI_TYPE: "Main VI"
DESCRIPTION: "LabVIEW module for controlling 1-axis linear stage via micromotion controller"

# FRONT PANEL CONTROLS
CONTROLS:
- COM Port: String input (default: "COM8")
- Connect Button: Boolean button
- Disconnect Button: Boolean button
- Position (steps): Numeric input (I32)
- Direction: Enum {Positive=125, Negative=175}
- Acceleration: Numeric input (U8, default: 0)
- Deceleration: Numeric input (U8, default: 0)
- Speed: Numeric input (I16, range: 5-4000)
- Move Button: Boolean button
- Set Speed Button: Boolean button
- Stop Button: Boolean button
- Home Button: Boolean button

# FRONT PANEL INDICATORS
INDICATORS:
- Connection Status: Boolean LED
- Current Position: Numeric indicator (I32)
- Movement Status: String indicator
- Error Status: String indicator
- Controller Ready: Boolean LED
- Limit Switch Status: String indicator

# BLOCK DIAGRAM STRUCTURE
BLOCK_DIAGRAM:
1. SERIAL CONFIGURATION:
   - VISA Configure Serial Port
   - Baud Rate: 19200
   - Data Bits: 8
   - Parity: None
   - Stop Bits: 1
   - Flow Control: None

2. CONTROLLER INITIALIZATION:
   - Send byte [100] to controller
   - Wait 100ms
   - Read response
   - Verify acknowledgment (expect 200)

3. MOVEMENT CONTROL:
   - Send byte [19] to initialize movement
   - Convert position to 3-byte sequence
   - Send XByte2, XByte1, XByte0 sequentially
   - Send direction byte
   - Send acceleration byte
   - Send deceleration byte
   - Check for completion acknowledgment (10)
   - Monitor status bytes (40=home limit, 41=far limit)
   - Send byte [163] to complete movement
   - Send three bytes [10] for finalization

4. SPEED CONTROL:
   - Send byte [34] to set speed
   - Convert speed to 2-byte hexadecimal
   - Send MSB and LSB
   - Send six bytes [0] for finalization

5. ERROR HANDLING:
   - VISA Error Handling
   - Timeout Management
   - Communication Error Detection
   - Limit Switch Detection

# SUB VIS
SUB_VIS:
- "Calculate_XByte_Sequence.vi": Converts position to 3-byte format
- "Send_Command_With_ACK.vi": Sends command and waits for acknowledgment
- "Check_Controller_Status.vi": Monitors controller status
- "Handle_Serial_Errors.vi": Error handling routine

# PROTOCOL IMPLEMENTATION
PROTOCOL_COMMANDS:
- Initialize: [100] -> Expect [200]
- Move Initiate: [19] -> Expect [10]
- Position Bytes: [XByte2][XByte1][XByte0]
- Direction: [125]=Positive, [175]=Negative
- Speed Set: [34] -> Expect [10]
- Movement Complete: [163]
- Finalize: [10][10][10]
- Stop: [104]

# TIMING REQUIREMENTS
TIMING:
- Wait time between commands: 100ms
- Serial timeout: 1000ms
- Movement timeout: User configurable

# DATA FORMATS
DATA_CONVERSIONS:
- Position: Decimal -> 6-digit hex -> 3 bytes
- Speed: Decimal -> 4-digit hex -> 2 bytes
- Direction: Enum -> Single byte
- Status: Byte -> String interpretation
